    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_AS_READ",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 0.98,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.04,
    "rationale": "I diluted the 18 h aliquot 10-fold and read it in duplicate. The two reads were 0.0991 and 0.0972, mean 0.0981. Scaled back by 10, that is about 0.98. The undiluted 18 h reading was 0.964. The two agree within about 2%, so the reader responds proportionally near 1.0 and is not saturated. If it were saturated, the diluted sample would have given a clearly higher back-calculated OD. The plateau at about 0.95 from 8 to 18 h therefore looks like real stationary phase and not signal compression. The abrupt flattening after the 7 h reading is consistent with nutrient limitation. Replicate agreement is good. Only the 18 h aliquot was tested, since the budget allowed one dilution and no earlier time point was read."
  },
